{#- Processing on the server (#382), shared by the viewer and the catalog.
    Two stages, driven by process.js: raw data in (a new radargram from the
    catalog, or a served one that has none yet), then steps in and a draft
    out. The viewer of a radargram with raw data starts at the second. -#}
{#- Read by `RIDAL.stepsEditor` (app.js) for the help under every steps box
    on the page, this dialog's and the /processing page's (#423). Here
    because every page with a steps box includes this dialog. An attribute,
    as `data-basemaps` is, so the template's own escaping makes it safe. -#}
<div id="step-catalog" data-steps="{{ step_catalog_json }}" hidden></div>
<dialog id="process-dialog" class="process-dialog">
  <h2 id="process-title">Process</h2>
  <p id="process-status" class="hint"></p>
  {#- Someone else processing this radargram (#382): said, not prevented. -#}
  <p id="process-activity" class="processing-activity" hidden></p>
  <section id="process-raw" hidden>
    <label id="process-id-label">Radargram id
      <input type="text" id="process-id" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
    </label>
    <p>
      <button type="button" id="process-choose">Choose raw files&hellip;</button>
      <input type="file" id="process-files" multiple hidden
             accept=".rad,.rd3,.rd7,.cor,.hd,.dt1,.gp2,.dzt,.dzg,.dzx">
    </p>
    <ul id="process-file-list" class="process-files"></ul>
    {#- Left empty, the positions go in the project's CRS when it sets one
        (`[processing] crs`), else in the UTM zone that suits them best, as
        `ridal process` does without `--crs`. process.js says which. -#}
    <label>CRS for the positions
      <input type="text" id="process-crs" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"
             placeholder="Automatic: the best UTM zone for the track">
    </label>
  </section>
  {#- The project's DEMs, uploaded on the Processing page. Like the profile
      select, process.js moves it: into the upload's choices, then above the
      recordings, where a change links the radargram at once. -#}
  <div id="process-dem-field" class="process-dem">
    <label>DEM
      <select id="process-dem">
        <option value="">None</option>
      </select>
    </label>
    <p class="hint">
      For the surface elevation along the track.
      <a href="{{ page_base|safe }}/processing#dems" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Add a DEM</a>
      on the Processing page.
    </p>
  </div>
  {#- What the recordings are, where their files do not say it or say it
      wrongly (#409). The source's, like the CRS and the DEM, so every
      draft and batch uses them. Moved as the DEM is: into the upload's
      choices, then above the recordings, where a change is saved at once.
      Empty reads them from the files. -#}
  <div id="process-antenna-field" class="process-antenna">
    <label>Antenna frequency (MHz)
      <input type="number" id="process-antenna-mhz" min="0" step="any"
             placeholder="From the files">
    </label>
    <label>Antenna separation (m)
      <input type="number" id="process-antenna-separation" min="0" step="any"
             placeholder="From the files">
    </label>
    <p class="hint">
      Only where the files do not say it, or say it wrongly. Empty reads it
      from the files.
    </p>
  </div>
  {#- In both stages: a new radargram can start in a profile, and one being
      processed can be moved to another. process.js moves it to where each
      stage wants it: here for the upload, just above the steps after. -#}
  <label id="process-profile-label">Processing profile
    <select id="process-profile">
      <option value="">None</option>
    </select>
  </label>
  <section id="process-draft">
    {#- Where the radargram stands against its processing profile, and the
        one-click way back to it when it is stale. -#}
    <div id="process-standing" class="process-standing" hidden>
      <p id="process-standing-text"></p>
      <button type="button" id="process-use-profile" hidden>Use the profile's steps</button>
    </div>
    <div id="process-dem-slot"></div>
    <div id="process-antenna-slot"></div>
    <ul id="process-recordings" class="process-files"></ul>
    {#- In the order they run: the radargram's own steps (only while it is
        in a profile), the profile, then the profile's steps. -#}
    <div id="process-pre" class="process-pre" hidden>
      <label class="process-steps">Steps before the profile, one per line
        <textarea id="process-pre-steps" rows="2" spellcheck="false"
                  placeholder="subset(0 2000)"></textarea>
      </label>
      <p class="hint">
        This radargram's own, run first. Only
        {% for step in step_catalog if step.pre_profile -%}
          {%- if not loop.first %}{% if loop.last %} and {% else %}, {% endif %}{% endif -%}
          <code>{{ step.name }}</code>
        {%- endfor %}.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div id="process-profile-slot"></div>
    {#- In a profile, its steps are folded away: they are the profile's,
        and changing them is a decision of its own. Outside one they are
        simply the steps, always open. -#}
    <details id="process-main" class="process-main" open>
      <summary id="process-main-summary"></summary>
      <p id="process-main-note" class="hint" hidden>
        These are the profile's. Changed here, they apply to this radargram
        only, and it will show as stale until it is processed with the
        profile's steps again.
      </p>
      <p class="process-steps-help">
        <button type="button" id="process-default-steps"
                data-steps="{{ default_processing_steps | join('\n') }}">Replace with default steps</button>
        <a href="{{ docs_base|safe }}reference/steps.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">All processing steps</a>
        &middot;
        <a href="{{ docs_base|safe }}guide/processing.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Processing guide</a>
      </p>
      <label class="process-steps">Steps, one per line
        <textarea id="process-steps" rows="8" spellcheck="false"
                  placeholder="As `ridal steps` lists them, e.g.&#10;zero_corr&#10;dewow&#10;bandpass(0.1 0.9)"></textarea>
      </label>
      <label>Medium velocity (m/ns)
        <input type="number" id="process-velocity" step="0.001" min="0.01" value="0.168">
      </label>
    </details>
  </section>
  <div id="process-error" class="warning" hidden></div>
  <figure id="process-result" class="process-result" hidden>
    {#- The render profiles, starting at the person's own. On a page with
        its own render profile select, process.js follows that instead. -#}
    <label>Render profile
      <select id="process-render">
        {%- for p in profiles %}
        <option value="{{ p }}" {% if p == active_profile %}selected{% endif %}>{{ p }}</option>
        {%- endfor %}
      </select>
    </label>
    <img id="process-image" alt="">
    <figcaption id="process-caption"></figcaption>
  </figure>
  <p id="process-headline"></p>
  <div id="process-detail"></div>
  {#- After applying steps that differ from the radargram's processing
      profile: make them the profile's next version, and process the
      profile's other radargrams with it. process.js fills it in. -#}
  <div id="process-offer" class="process-offer" hidden>
    <p id="process-offer-text"></p>
    <p>
      <button type="button" id="process-offer-yes"></button>
      <button type="button" id="process-offer-no">No, only this radargram</button>
    </p>
  </div>
  {#- What is happening now, beside the buttons that started it, both kept
      in view at the foot of the dialog however long it has grown. -#}
  <div class="process-footer">
  <p id="process-progress" class="hint" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <p>
    <button type="button" id="process-upload" hidden disabled>Upload</button>
    <button type="button" id="process-cancel-upload" hidden>Cancel upload</button>
    <button type="button" id="process-run">Process</button>
    <button type="button" id="process-toggle" hidden>Show current</button>
    <button type="button" id="process-commit" hidden>Apply and close</button>
    <button type="button" id="process-confirm" class="danger" hidden>Apply anyway and close</button>
    {#- Cancel, not Close: closing throws away a draft that was not applied. -#}
    <button type="button" id="process-close">Cancel</button>
  </p>
  </div>
</dialog>
